                <h2>Expert Care for Eczema & Psoriasis</h2>
                <p>Eczema and psoriasis are chronic inflammatory skin conditions that can significantly impact your quality of life. At Smart Skin Dermatology, our board-certified dermatologists specialize in diagnosing and treating these conditions with the latest evidence-based approaches.</p>
                
                <h3>Understanding Eczema (Atopic Dermatitis)</h3>
                <p>Eczema causes patches of skin to become red, inflamed, itchy, and sometimes cracked or rough. It often appears in childhood but can develop at any age. Common triggers include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Environmental allergens (dust, pollen, pet dander)</li>
                    <li>Harsh soaps and detergents</li>
                    <li>Stress and anxiety</li>
                    <li>Weather changes and dry air</li>
                    <li>Certain foods</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Understanding Psoriasis</h3>
                <p>Psoriasis is an autoimmune condition that causes cells to build up rapidly on the skin's surface, forming scales and red patches that can be itchy and sometimes painful. Types we treat include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Plaque Psoriasis:</strong> The most common type, causing raised, red patches covered with silvery scales</li>
                    <li><strong>Guttate Psoriasis:</strong> Small, dot-like lesions, often triggered by strep infections</li>
                    <li><strong>Inverse Psoriasis:</strong> Smooth, red patches in skin folds</li>
                    <li><strong>Pustular Psoriasis:</strong> White pustules surrounded by red skin</li>
                    <li><strong>Scalp Psoriasis:</strong> Affecting the scalp with thick, crusted plaques</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Our Treatment Approach</h3>
                <p>We offer comprehensive treatment options tailored to your specific condition and lifestyle:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Topical Treatments:</strong> Prescription-strength corticosteroids, calcineurin inhibitors, and vitamin D analogues</li>
                    <li><strong>Phototherapy:</strong> Controlled UV light therapy to reduce inflammation</li>
                    <li><strong>Systemic Medications:</strong> Oral or injectable medications for moderate to severe cases</li>
                    <li><strong>Biologic Therapies:</strong> Advanced targeted treatments for psoriasis</li>
                    <li><strong>Lifestyle Counseling:</strong> Identifying and avoiding triggers</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>What to Expect at Your Appointment</h3>
                <p>During your visit, we will:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Conduct a thorough examination of affected areas</li>
                    <li>Review your medical history and current symptoms</li>
                    <li>Discuss potential triggers and aggravating factors</li>
                    <li>Create a personalized treatment plan</li>
                    <li>Provide education on proper skincare routines</li>
                </ul>
