        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is eczema contagious?</h3>
            <p>No, eczema is not contagious. It cannot be spread from person to person. It's related to genetics and immune system function.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Can psoriasis be cured?</h3>
            <p>While there's no cure for psoriasis, it can be effectively managed with proper treatment. Many patients achieve clear or nearly clear skin with the right therapy.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How long does treatment take to work?</h3>
            <p>Results vary depending on the treatment and severity. Topical treatments may show improvement in 2-4 weeks, while biologics may take 3-4 months for full effect.</p>
